# 2. Mutation run: each of 242 deliberate changes applied alone to a scratch copy. Script: outputs/mutate-monitoring.sh   Output: outputs/mutation-run.txt
$ for i in 0 1 2 3 4 5; do TERRAFORM=<terraform> PART=$i/6 bash outputs/mutate-monitoring.sh <worktree> & done      (six parts, each runs every sixth mutation)
Baseline 104 of 104 pass on the unmutated tree. Mutations 242 (181 exact-string changes whose old text is found exactly once, checked first with COUNT_ONLY=1, and 61 pattern changes): caught 242, not caught 0.
A change counts as caught only when the changed file still parses (node --check, bash -n, terraform fmt, an ini line check) and at least one case fails by name; NOOP, AMBIGUOUS, INVALID, CRASH, HUNG and SURVIVED are reported as not caught.
History: the first run (244 changes, 92 cases) left 18 not caught. Cases were added for the properties they showed (a running unit taken for a good tick, the state file version, ages rounded up, the order of the lookups under the cap, a vanished pipeline, a finish in the future, the exact-token redaction by the logger itself, the GitLab retry, an option value that is an option, a stale queue next to a failed read, a stopped agent, an agent that does not start), four pieces of redundant code were removed (a second clamp of finish times, a stored-time validation that collectTicks repeats, dpkg -E, a .catch that Promise.race makes unnecessary) and their mutations dropped or replaced. The recorded run is the last, against the final tests and code.

